@title PCSA00015 front end - title screen, GAME MODE, campaign intro, campaign map
@game  PCSA00015
# (no cadence shots - every shot below is explicit)

# ============================================================================
# WHAT THIS RECIPE DOES
# Boots the title and drives its TOUCH front end as far as it currently goes:
#
#   loading -> PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START -> GAME MODE (4 tiles)
#     -> SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN -> the campaign intro text -> the campaign MAP
#
# Every input here was found in a resident session and is reproducible; the
# shots below are the evidence for each screen.
#
# >>> IT NEEDS `VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0`, AND THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL.
# With the default per-flip clock top-up, a displayed frame carries about a
# TENTH of the guest work a console frame carries (measured: 3120 fps with
# barely one whole scheduler quantum per frame), so this title never finishes
# loading at all - a 300,000-frame run ends still on the loading screen. With
# the top-up off it reaches PRESS ANY BUTTON by f30000. See
# `VitaState::advance_time_frame` for the mechanism and why it is a knob rather
# than the default.
#
#   VITASLOP_FRAME_TOPUP=0 play --game <dir> --recipe <this> --max-frames 40000
#
# THE TITLE IS TOUCH-DRIVEN, and this recipe is the proof: the four GAME MODE
# tiles, the confirm checkmark and the map's own back button all respond to a
# `touch=`, and `cross` works on the two screens that say "press any button".
# `touch=X,Y` is in PANEL coordinates, which are screen*2.
#
# >>> WHERE IT STOPS, AND WHY - read this before extending it
# The campaign MAP renders its HUD and nothing else, and it is FROZEN: the
# scene digest is bit-identical over 25,000 frames, and a 4x4 grid of taps
# across the whole map body produces the SAME digest as no input at all. The
# nodes the intro text tells you to touch are not there to be touched.
#
# Two measured facts about that, so the next session does not re-derive them:
#   1. The map's geometry IS being submitted - one pass carries 20,160 world
#      triangles - but its render target is a 1x1 colour surface (the title
#      really does init it 1x1 with stride 8, which is GXM's legal minimum), so
#      nothing of it reaches the display. Only the 27-draw HUD pass targets the
#      960x544 surface.
#   2. There is NO game-logic thread left. `threads` at the map lists the
#      render thread, audio, the FIOS workers and one "NEW THREAD" blocked on a
#      semaphore that nothing signals. The main thread is gone.
# So the map is a STALL to diagnose, not a screen to find the right tap for.
# ============================================================================

0: @section boot
# No input while it loads. This is the boot ladder of boot.recipe, unchanged.

28000: cross
28000: @shot title-screen
28020:
# "PRESS ANY BUTTON TO START" -> GAME MODE

28620: touch=472,524
28620: @shot game-mode
28640:
# The SINGLE PLAYER CAMPAIGN tile (screen 236,262). The two greyed tiles are
# ONLINE CAMPAIGN and CROSS-PLAY - this build is signed out, so they are
# correctly unavailable.

29040: cross
29040: @shot campaign-intro
29060:
# The intro text ("Touch the nodes to play events"). `cross` brings up its
# confirm checkmark rather than dismissing it.

29460: touch=1760,952
29460: @shot campaign-intro-confirm
29480:
# The checkmark, bottom right (screen 880,476).

33000: @section campaign-map
33000: @shot campaign-map

# @todo The map is frozen - see the header. Next: find who should signal the
# semaphore "NEW THREAD" waits on, and why the map pass targets a 1x1 surface.
# @todo No @assert yet: the map has no progress value, and the screens above
# are only evidenced by their shots. The first assertable thing here would be a
# watch on whatever the front end advances when a node is selected.
